From: Gerson Fernando Budke <gerson.budke@ossystems.com.br>
Subject: [PATCH] STM32_ADC_Common: Select adc has enhance sampling selection

Signed-off-by: Gerson Fernando Budke <gerson.budke@ossystems.com.br>

Ported to Renode v1.17.0 STM32_ADC_Common API.
Upstream SamplingTime.TwoSelections already models the SMP1/SMP2 +
per-channel SMPSELx layout, so the hasEnhanceSamplingTime constructor
parameter is not reintroduced (C0/G0/WBA use TwoSelections). The
remaining part of the change, making SMP1/SMP2 readable back, is applied
to the TwoSelections register layout.

diff --git a/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Analog/STM32_ADC_Common.cs b/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Analog/STM32_ADC_Common.cs
--- a/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Analog/STM32_ADC_Common.cs
+++ b/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Analog/STM32_ADC_Common.cs
@@ @@ private void BuildSampingTimeRegisters(Dictionary<long, DoubleWordRegister> regi
             {
                 /* SMP1 and SMP2 defined in 0-2 and 4-6, other bits from 8 to 8 + channelCount are
                  * to select SMP1 or SMP2.
+                 * SMP1 and SMP2 values are not used by the model, but software expects to read them back.
                  */
                 var smpr = new DoubleWordRegister(this)
-                    .WithTag("SMP1", 0, 3)
+                    .WithValueField(0, 3, name: "SMP1")
                     .WithReservedBits(3, 1)
-                    .WithTag("SMP2", 4, 3)
+                    .WithValueField(4, 3, name: "SMP2")
                     .WithReservedBits(7, 1);
                 for(int i = 0; i < ADCChannelCount; i++)
                 {
